FFmpeg 9.0.2 Vulkan encoders (on top of codecs-enc1's libavcodec: decode 0001/0002, consecutive-b-frames-all, dyadic
reference pattern, and the AV1 CDEF-under-RC patch): multiple P references, H.264 reference list modifications, and
an AV1 B pyramid.

hw_base_encode:
 - P-pictures reference the last p_refs top-layer pictures (anchors), nearest first = the default H.264/H.265 list
   order; p_refs = ref_l0 for AV1 (as before) and, for the other codecs, when -refs asks for it (upstream TODO
   "apply both previous and forward multi reference for all vaapi encoders"). The older anchors stay in the DPB of
   the B-pictures in between; anchors restart at every intra picture (H.265 trailing pictures).
 - H.264 max_num_ref_frames / max_dec_frame_buffering and H.265 max_dec_pic_buffering count those references.
 - AV1 repeat frames (show_existing_frame tails) are queued, several at a time, and each is sent once every picture
   before it in display order has been output (a pyramid has several hidden frames pending).
vulkan_encode:
 - several hidden frames are kept and sent, in coding order, in the temporal unit of the next shown frame (was one:
   assert !prev_buf_ref).
 - a DPB slot is reused once its picture is no longer referenced by a picture still to be coded (and is not a
   forward reference of the next P); the picture itself may stay alive longer for DPB bookkeeping. A 7-B pyramid
   needs more pictures in flight than anv's 9 AV1 DPB slots.
vulkan_encode_h264:
 - refList0/1ModOpCount is the number of modification operations (was one less, dropping the last).
 - num_ref_idx_active_override_flag whenever the active counts differ from the PPS defaults.
vulkan_encode_h265:
 - every reference is active (was forced to the PPS default, one), with num_ref_idx_active_override_flag set after
   setup_slices() (which reset it).
vulkan_encode_av1:
 - reference frame slots (VBI) are allocated: a referenced picture (P, or a B in a pyramid) refreshes a slot whose
   frame neither stays in its DPB nor still waits to be shown (was: P toggled between slots 0 and 1, B never
   refreshed); ref_order_hint[] carries every slot's order hint; P names its nearest reference LAST and the next
   GOLDEN by display order.
 - show_frame: a frame is shown when coded only if every frame before it in display order is already coded (the
   encode/display index comparison shows pyramid B frames out of order after a closed GOP).

